{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe task is DATA-HDB-01. I need to implement a `solve(case)` function that computes the Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) using mutual reachability distances (which is the core of HDBSCAN's MST step).\n\nThe mutual reachability distance between two points u and v is:\n`mreach(u, v) = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], distance(u, v))`\n\nThen I need to find the MST of the complete graph with these mutual reachability distances.\n\nThe output should be:\n- `mst_edges`: list of [node1, node2, weight] triples\n- `total_weight`: sum of edge weights\n\nLet me implement Kruskal's or Prim's algorithm.\n\nFor each edge (u, v, d) in distances, compute the mutual reachability distance:\n`mr_d = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)`\n\nThen run MST (Kruskal's) on these reweighted edges.\n\nLet me verify with case 0:\n- core_distance: p0=0.23243377, p1=0.50398147, p2=0.55673811, p3=0.66828478, p4=0.43968915\n\nEdges with mutual reachability:\n- p0-p1: max(0.23243377, 0.50398147, 0.89672724) = 0.89672724\n- p0-p2: max(0.23243377, 0.55673811, 0.73968893) = 0.73968893\n- p0-p3: max(0.23243377, 0.66828478, 0.77270596) = 0.77270596\n- p0-p4: max(0.23243377, 0.43968915, 0.87376631) = 0.87376631\n- p1-p2: max(0.50398147, 0.55673811, 1.08418122) = 1.08418122\n- p1-p3: max(0.50398147, 0.66828478, 0.82719237) = 0.82719237\n- p1-p4: max(0.50398147, 0.43968915, 0.61293041) = 0.61293041\n- p2-p3: max(0.55673811, 0.66828478, 1.00286271) = 1.00286271\n- p2-p4: max(0.55673811, 0.43968915, 0.5322912) = 0.55673811\n- p3-p4: max(0.66828478, 0.43968915, 0.51351834) = 0.66828478\n\nSorted edges:\n- p2-p4: 0.55673811\n- p3-p4: 0.66828478\n- p1-p4: 0.61293041\n- p0-p2: 0.73968893\n- p0-p3: 0.77270596\n- p1-p3: 0.82719237\n- p0-p4: 0.87376631\n- p0-p1: 0.89672724\n- p2-p3: 1.00286271\n- p1-p2: 1.08418122\n\nWait, let me sort properly:\n0.55673811 (p2-p4)\n0.61293041 (p1-p4)\n0.66828478 (p3-p4)\n0.73968893 (p0-p2)\n0.77270596 (p0-p3)\n0.82719237 (p1-p3)\n0.87376631 (p0-p4)\n0.89672724 (p0-p1)\n1.00286271 (p2-p3)\n1.08418122 (p1-p2)\n\nKruskal's:\n1. p2-p4: 0.55673811 → add (components: {p2,p4}, {p0}, {p1}, {p3})\n2. p1-p4: 0.61293041 → add (components: {p1,p2,p4}, {p0}, {p3})\n3. p3-p4: 0.66828478 → add (components: {p1,p2,p3,p4}, {p0})\n4. p0-p2: 0.73968893 → add (connects p0 to the large component)\n\nMST edges: p2-p4, p1-p4, p3-p4, p0-p2\nTotal: 0.55673811 + 0.61293041 + 0.66828478 + 0.73968893 = 2.57764223\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    core_distance = case[\"core_distance\"]\n    distances = case[\"distances\"]\n    \n    # Compute mutual reachability distances\n    mr_edges = []\n    for u, v, d in distances:\n        mr_d = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\n        mr_edges.append((mr_d, u, v))\n    \n    # Sort by mutual reachability distance\n    mr_edges.sort()\n    \n    # Kruskal's MST with Union-Find\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n    \n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        parent[ry] = rx\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    mst_edges = []\n    total_weight = 0.0\n    \n    for mr_d, u, v in mr_edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, mr_d])\n            total_weight += mr_d\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\n                break\n    \n    return {\"mst_edges\": mst_edges, \"total_weight\": total_weight}\n```\n\nThis looks correct. The response must be a JSON object with a single key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    core_distance = case[\\\"core_distance\\\"]\\n    distances = case[\\\"distances\\\"]\\n\\n    # Compute mutual reachability distance for each edge\\n    mr_edges = []\\n    for entry in distances:\\n        u, v, d = entry[0], entry[1], entry[2]\\n        mr_d = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d)\\n        mr_edges.append((mr_d, u, v))\\n\\n    # Sort edges by mutual reachability distance (Kruskal's)\\n    mr_edges.sort()\\n\\n    # Union-Find\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\\n        parent[ry] = rx\\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n\\n    for mr_d, u, v in mr_edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, mr_d])\\n            total_weight += mr_d\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n\\n    return {\\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges, \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight}\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01BZ9k94WkQ3UqRn8Q0hHhzy","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2078},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2078,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":59,"output_tokens":2062,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1611},"service_tier":"standard"}}